Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["\<\
The missing piece -- the escape-probability weight correction\
\>", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"ea9cb103-c78e-40d2-912a-6a5e0875e48d"],

Cell["\<\
exitProbDist/ePDFx/eCDFx above give the corrected sampling distribution for \
the exit direction, assuming escape is certain. But a walk sampled from the \
ordinary mixed classical/Dwivedi-guided scheme has no such guarantee. \
Substituting the corrected direction in without correcting for that mismatch \
introduces a bias equal to exactly how likely the original scheme was to have \
escaped from this same depth. This section works that probability out, so the \
resampled contribution can be divided by it and come out unbiased.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"7a1f2e72-85d6-49f0-9519-be08387b1bf7"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Classical (unguided) escape probability -- closed form", "Subsection",ExpressionUUID->"c4ebdf3c-7be0-4e71-8b0d-a2b60e621896"],

Cell["\<\
P(escape | classical sampling, depth x) = Integrate[(1/2) Exp[x/u], \
{u,-1,0}], which reduces exactly to (1/2) E2(x) via u -> -1/s.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"6d0722f2-7518-4149-9d53-6f2ae32fa4ab"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["\<\
PescClassical[x_?NumericQ]:=(1/2) ExpIntegralE[2,N[x]];

(* sanity check: numeric value at a few depths *)
Table[{x, PescClassical[x] // N}, {x, {0.2, 0.5, 1.0, 2.0, 5.0}}]\
\>", "Input",
 CellChangeTimes->{3.996660848002322*^9},
 CellLabel->
  "In[288]:=",ExpressionUUID->"b49da841-2667-4ba6-926c-0116998dd401"],

